WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.750
- I'd like to also touch on a subject

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:03.040
that I think many doctors

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:05.480
and health organizations
are avoiding talking about

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.770
and that's how protests are
affecting COVID-19 numbers.

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:12.610
If you know me at all, I am
not a fan of fear-mongering.

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.420
You've heard me call out the
media time and time again

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:18.050
about the fact that they're
only after clicks and viewership

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:19.840
with the type of
fear-mongering they put out.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.220
But I think it's about time

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:23.150
that I fear-monger you a little bit.

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:25.810
I gave us so much credit as
a nation in the beginning,

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:27.780
I would go on nationwide TV shows

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.890
and say there's so much
unity around COVID.

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:31.670
And now, I don't know what happened

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:33.140
over these last few weeks

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:35.430
but we threw social
distancing out the window.

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:37.300
We threw masks out the window

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.780
and we're no longer being alert,

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:40.290
we're no longer being proactive.

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:41.150
And what's happening?

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:44.310
COVID cases are spiking, people are dying,

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:47.120
and the second wave isn't even here yet.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:51.500
18 states are experiencing
new highs of COVID-19 cases.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.360
Six states have a spike greater
than 50% in their cases.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:56.870
This is a huge problem folks.

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:59.080
Because the way we control COVID right now

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:01.730
is by being responsible, both you and me.

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:04.350
And that means keeping
six feet away from others.

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:06.160
That means wearing a mask at all times

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:07.630
where you're encountering other people.

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:10.020
Recently, I took a walk
around New York City

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:11.260
and I saw bars open.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:13.020
I saw people standing next to each other,

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:15.080
talking with no masks in groups of 50.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:16.180
We can't do this,

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:19.070
because the more we do it the
more people are gonna suffer,

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:20.850
especially because we
don't have a vaccine.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.170
If you think it's bad now,

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.080
it can get a lot worse for the fall.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:25.420
Many people have asked me

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:28.650
if vaccines are the answer to COVID-19

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.580
and while I have high
hopes for the vaccine,

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:32.270
I also have a few reservations.

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:35.820
Dr. Fauci, NIH, CDC have said
that the proposed timeline

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:38.180
if everything goes well early, 2021,

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:40.230
and that's the fastest
we've ever had a vaccine.

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:42.060
So while I'm hopeful it comes out then,

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:44.210
it's very easy for something to go wrong.

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:45.610
The vaccine not get created,

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:48.380
we see some harmful effects
and the timeline gets pushed.

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:51.010
Second, we don't know yet
the efficacy of this vaccine

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:53.020
because while there are several companies,

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:55.580
several trials, and several
different vaccines in play,

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:57.270
we don't know yet what percentage

00:01:57.270 --> 00:01:59.410
of the time do these
vaccines actually work.

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:03.010
That is why I'm still urging
you to socially distance,

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:05.210
to wear a mask, to wash your hands

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:07.270
because you could be
standing next to someone

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:08.690
who looks completely healthy

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:10.790
and they could potentially
be getting you sick.

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:12.560
And going even further on this topic,

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:15.540
I wanna discuss something
that the WHO has said

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:17.360
which has made my blood boil.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:20.460
The WHO issued this statement last week

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:22.510
and it confused a lot of people.

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:23.343
Take a listen.

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:24.180
- From the data we have,

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:25.420
it still seems to be rare

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:29.380
that an asymptomatic person
actually transmits onward

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:31.360
to a secondary individual.

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:34.650
- This confused everybody, even doctors.

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:35.820
We were all confused

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:38.090
as to which research
they were talking about.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.610
Most people, like Joe
Rogan took it this way.

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:42.730
- Now this comes out today that was,

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:44.570
it basically said if you're asymptomatic,

00:02:44.570 --> 00:02:46.960
you can't transfer it as
easily as they thought.

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:48.030
It's almost impossible.

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:48.863
- So all that worry

00:02:48.863 --> 00:02:50.930
that we were about kids giving
it to their grandmothers,

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:51.763
they're not gonna do that.

00:02:51.763 --> 00:02:53.830
- That was the only reason
why stores are shut down.

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:57.830
- This is a prime example of
poor scientific communication.

00:02:57.830 --> 00:02:58.670
Let me explain.

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:01.620
Asymptomatic means something
different in technical terms

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:02.820
than it does to you or I.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:04.810
This researcher was trying to explain

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:06.870
that those who are asymptomatic,

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:08.610
meaning aren't showing symptoms right now,

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:11.530
and will never show symptoms
don't usually spread COVID

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:13.520
but pre-symptomatic patients,

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:15.760
those who are asymptomatic right now

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:19.270
but will get sick later can
spread COVID quite quickly.

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:21.100
To scientists, pre-symptomatic

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.910
and asymptomatic are two different terms.

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:24.970
To you and I, they're the same thing.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.380
The WHO quickly corrected this statement

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:30.160
and I understood the mistake
that they made, it happens.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:33.500
As a large organization, that
is general-public-facing,

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:36.020
they need to do a better job
at clarifying these things.

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:38.230
We need to be able to trust the WHO.

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:41.200
I've consistently said on
this channel to trust the WHO.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:42.733
YouTube pushes you to the WHO.

00:03:42.733 --> 00:03:44.130
- Anything that would go

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:46.460
against World Health
Organization recommendations

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:47.670
would be a violation of our policy.

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:49.890
- So we need to not lose trust in them.

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:50.960
And the way that we do that

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:53.330
is for them to avoid mistakes
like this in the future.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:55.860
And speaking of mistakes,
let's talk about my advice

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:57.790
on masks early on in this pandemic.

00:03:57.790 --> 00:04:01.310
Here's a clip of me from
mid-February talking about masks

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:04.030
and pay close attention
to the words that I use.

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:05.680
The CDC has been firm on this.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:07.710
Most people, the ones that are healthy

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:10.330
and not sick do not need
a mask at this time.

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:12.198
Notice that I approached that subject

00:04:12.198 --> 00:04:13.730
with a level of humility.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:16.000
I wasn't certain that masks wouldn't help.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.270
The best evidence at the time told us

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:20.490
that masks wouldn't help
and it was true then;

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:22.470
however, now we know something different,

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:23.760
and that something different is

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:25.300
just because someone is healthy

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:27.370
doesn't mean they can't
be spreading the virus.

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:28.830
In the beginning of this pandemic,

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:31.240
people thought by wearing
masks they'd protect themselves

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:32.810
so we said, "No, that's wrong,"

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:35.520
but now we recommend
masks not to protect you,

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:36.860
the person wearing the mask,

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:39.410
but to limit you, as a
person who looks healthy,

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:41.370
from spreading the virus
into the environment.

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:42.880
So by everyone wearing a mask,

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:45.360
we're protecting the
community not the wearer.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:47.520
In addition, in the
beginning of the pandemic,

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:50.160
we had a huge shortage of surgical masks

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:52.550
and N95 masks in the hospital setting

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:55.570
where we were working directly
with COVID-19 patients,

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:58.150
and medical providers were
dying as a result of that.

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:00.520
I still stand by my guidance at the time

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:01.860
even though it wasn't accurate.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:04.040
It was based off the best
evidence at the time.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:04.873
Will it change?

00:05:04.873 --> 00:05:05.706
Yes.

00:05:05.706 --> 00:05:07.610
Will I be afraid to tell
you that it's changed?

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:10.240
No, because I want you
to constantly be updated.

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:12.080
Looking at the most recent research,

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.419
we've seen that actually wearing masks,

00:05:14.419 --> 00:05:16.830
even that cheap and
expensive surgical masks

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:19.560
or fabric face coverings
really does limit the spread

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:21.140
of this specific virus.

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:23.420
That's why it upsets me so
to walk around New York City

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:25.470
and see all these people not wearing masks

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:26.640
when they're in crowds of people.

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:28.450
Look, if you're walking
out into your backyard

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:30.350
and no one's there, you don't need a mask.

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:31.690
If you live in a remote area

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:32.690
where you're not gonna run into anybody,

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:34.440
you don't need a mask; however,

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:36.730
if you're going out to a crowded area,

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:38.100
you have to wear a mask.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.358
I'd like to also touch on a subject

00:05:39.358 --> 00:05:41.010
that I think many doctors

00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:43.450
and health organizations
are avoiding talking about,

00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:46.790
and that's how protests are
affecting COVID-19 numbers.

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:49.410
We can't, as health care institutions,

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:52.587
go out and say, "Hey do not
have any social gatherings

00:05:52.587 --> 00:05:55.650
"unless you're protesting a just cause."

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:57.290
We can't say that, that's not accurate.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:06:00.390
If you have a huge social
gathering of thousands of people,

00:06:00.390 --> 00:06:01.650
you're putting your life at risk

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:03.990
and potentially the lives
of who you will encounter

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:05.100
throughout your next days.

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:06.130
When you're protesting,

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:08.470
try and keep six feet away from others.

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:09.920
If you're gonna be chanting or singing,

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:11.860
make sure the mask is covering your face.

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:14.390
For the next two weeks
do your best to stay away

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:17.460
from vulnerable populations:
those over the age of 60

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:19.240
or with immunocompromised states.

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:22.350
And after you protest, please,
please, go and get tested.

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:23.930
Because the last thing we want you to do

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:26.130
is to be one of those
people who are asymptomatic

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:28.190
or pre-symptomatic and
are spreading this virus

00:06:28.190 --> 00:06:29.420
to thousands of people.

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:32.030
The virus unfortunately, doesn't care

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:34.620
if there are racial injustices
occurring in this country.

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:37.010
I hate that these racial
injustice is occurring.

00:06:37.010 --> 00:06:39.440
The medical community
stands with the protests

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:41.860
but we have to be objective and still say

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:44.260
that by protesting you're
putting your life at risk.

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:46.330
Look, I get it, we're burned out.

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:49.440
We've been sitting at home
for close to three months now,

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:52.070
not being able to go do
the things that we enjoy,

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:53.900
not being able to see our loved ones,

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:57.130
not being able to find work
and struggling to pay rent

00:06:57.130 --> 00:06:58.780
and securing food, I get it.

00:06:58.780 --> 00:07:01.410
What you're experiencing
is called caution fatigue.

00:07:01.410 --> 00:07:03.030
There's even a medical term for it

00:07:03.030 --> 00:07:04.650
and we in the medical community experience

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:06.640
something similar called alarm fatigue.

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:08.950
We're in the ER and there's
constant alarm bells ringing,

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:11.110
we stopped paying attention
to them and that's a problem.

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:12.580
I think media constantly giving you

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:14.310
an outbreak warning every single day,

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:16.500
telling you that there's a
new coronavirus high number

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:18.920
has burned you out to the
point where you tune it out

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:21.430
and that's a problem because
I need you to stay alert

00:07:21.430 --> 00:07:24.200
but I also need you to
stay active not anxious.

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:26.490
I recommended a couple of
videos for you here to watch

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:28.760
and as always, stay happy and healthy.

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:31.427
(upbeat music)

